course: dictionary
lesson: 1163
title: Words with more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. When you meet one, use the context to choose the right meaning. The word bristly can describe a hedgehog's back, a rough brush, or a grumpy person.
explain: «Dad's chin is bristly before he shaves.» The sentence is about hair growing on a chin, so bristly means covered with short, stiff hairs. Try the meaning in the sentence: "Dad's chin is covered with short, stiff hairs before he shaves." It makes sense.
explain: «A bristly old man may be grumpy.» A man is not covered in hair here, and grumpy is a clue. So bristly means easily annoyed or quick to get angry. This is the informal meaning, used in everyday talk and stories.
explain: Always ask: which meaning fits this sentence? Swap your choice into the sentence. If it still sounds right, you have found the meaning the writer wanted.
fact: Bristly means covered with short, stiff hairs, or stiff and rough like bristles.
fact: In informal speech, bristly means easily annoyed or quick to get angry.
fact: Bristly is an adjective. Its comparative forms are bristlier and bristliest.
fact: Real biology: the biggest whales, such as blue and humpback whales, have no teeth but baleen, rows of bristly plates in the mouth.
fact: Baleen sieves tiny shrimp-like krill and small fish out of the water, a bit like a real grating.
exercise: «Dad's chin is bristly before he shaves.» What does bristly mean here? | Sweet-smelling | Very hot to touch | *Covered with short, stiff hairs | Soft and smooth like silk
exercise: «A bristly old man may be grumpy.» Which meaning fits here? | *Easily annoyed or quick to get angry | Giving out light | Very old | Covered with short, stiff hairs
exercise: Mia says a bristly brush must be soft. Why is she wrong? | *Bristly means stiff and rough like bristles | Bristly means quiet | Bristly means very hot | Bristly means soft and smooth
test: Dad says his chin is ___ before he shaves. | cold | sleepy | *bristly | silky
test: Which animal is bristly? | frog | *hedgehog | snail | goldfish
exam: Grandma says, "Don't bother him, he's bristly today." What does bristly mean here? | *Easily annoyed or quick to get angry | Stiff and rough like a brush | Giving out light | Covered with short, stiff hairs
